Abstract
The emergence of manycore embedded systems, for example, has triggered the development of interconnect architectures to support efficient communication between manycores within a single chip. In particular, a Network-on-Chip (NoC) has emerged as a powerful solution for interconnecting multiple components in a many-core systems. Thus, the need for an early design space exploration (DSE) for many-core NoC becomes significant to evaluate different architectural parameters. As such, the work presented in this paper introduces an early DSE approach for many-core NoC. The proposed DSE approach considers many architectural parameters for many-core NoC including topology, routing algorithm, buffer

